{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":950777,"ns":0,"title":"Analytic signal","extract":"In mathematics and signal processing, an analytic signal is a complex-valued function that has no negative frequency components. The real and imaginary parts of an analytic signal are real-valued functions related to each other by the Hilbert transform.","description":"Particular representation of a signal","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}